### ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()

Source: https://gsap.com/docs/v3/Plugins/ScrollTrigger/static.matchMedia%28%29

Creates ScrollTrigger animations that are active only when the specified media query matches. Automatically kills ScrollTriggers when the breakpoint no longer matches, and supports optional teardown functions for custom cleanup.

```APIDOC
## ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()

### Description
Creates ScrollTrigger animations that are active only when the specified media query matches. Automatically kills ScrollTriggers when the breakpoint no longer matches, and supports optional teardown functions for custom cleanup.

### Method
`ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()`

### Syntax
`ScrollTrigger.matchMedia(vars)`

### Parameters
- **vars** (Object) - Required - An object where keys are media query strings (e.g., "(min-width: 800px)") or the special key "all", and values are functions that create animations. Each function can optionally return a teardown function.

### Usage Example
```javascript
ScrollTrigger.matchMedia({
  // desktop
  "(min-width: 800px)": function () {
    gsap.to(".panel", {
      xPercent: -100,
      scrollTrigger: {
        trigger: ".panel",
        scrub: 1,
        pin: true,
        end: "+=500",
      },
    });
  },

  // mobile
  "(max-width: 799px)": function () {
    gsap.to("#logo", {
      scale: 0.5,
      scrollTrigger: {
        trigger: ".nav-bar",
        start: "top top",
        toggleActions: "play none reverse none",
      },
    });
  },

  // all
  all: function () {
    gsap.set(".photo", { opacity: 0 });
    ScrollTrigger.batch(".photo", {
      onEnter: (elements) =>
        gsap.to(elements, { opacity: 1, stagger: 0.1, overwrite: true }),
    });
  },
});
```

### Teardown Function
You can optionally return a function from any media query callback. This function will be called when that breakpoint no longer matches, allowing you to perform custom cleanup routines (e.g., killing non-ScrollTrigger animations). ScrollTriggers created inside the callback are automatically killed, so the teardown is only needed for other animations.

#### Example with Teardown
```javascript
ScrollTrigger.matchMedia({
  "(min-width: 800px)": function () {
    // ScrollTrigger (automatically killed when breakpoint no longer matches)
    gsap.to(".panel", {
      xPercent: -100,
      scrollTrigger: {
        trigger: ".panel",
        scrub: 1,
        end: "+=500",
      },
    });

    // other animations that aren't ScrollTrigger-related...
    let tl = gsap.timeline();
    tl.to(".box", { rotation: 360 }).to(".box", { y: 100 });

    // Return a function to clean up when breakpoint no longer matches
    return function () {
      tl.kill();
      // other cleanup code can go here.
    };
  },
});
```

### Notes
- ScrollTrigger automatically kills all ScrollTriggers created inside the media query function when that media query no longer matches.
- The animation associated with a ScrollTrigger will be killed along with the ScrollTrigger when the media query no longer matches.
- Any (or all) of the media queries can return a teardown function.
- For mobile devices, ensure you have the viewport meta tag: `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">`.
- `ScrollTrigger.matchMedia()` was added in GSAP 3.4.0. The teardown return function capability was added in 3.5.0.
```

